# 4.2.scenario.elimination.assay.rank.stone

## .what

rank the enumerated tests by **separation-power × (1/cost)** — with a **catastrophic-branch
priority** override: a test that rules out a live can't-miss landmine jumps the queue regardless of
its cost, because the veto it lifts is worth it.

## .inputs

- `4.1.scenario.elimination.assay.enumerate.yield.md` — the test-per-scenario map
- `3.3.scenario.disentangle.correlation.blend.yield.md` — the scenario severities

## .do

- score each test by how many scenarios it separates (power) against its cost/invasiveness/time
- apply the override: a test that rules out a **live catastrophic** scenario ranks first — it lifts a
  treatment veto (per `rule.require.superposition-until-elimination`)
- note tests that close a cheap knowledge gap (an owner question) — near-free, rank high

## .emit

into `4.2.scenario.elimination.assay.rank.yield.md` — the ranked test list.

## .done when

tests are ranked by power × cost, with catastrophic-branch tests prioritized, cheap gap-closers noted.
